\item[* task:] to substitute a subordinate adverbial clause for its variable.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals) It is assumed 
for the moment that the sentence always remains in postsentadvrel, and that a 
separating comma is not obligatory, although it is allowed in 
analysis (so reversed from the situation of an initial subsentence!). 
No substorder condition is needed, since the sub-sentence is sentence final.
Temporal sentences of course should not be substituted here, but in 
the tempadvsentsubst rules.

The condition on declaratives has been formulated since wh-open infinitives
cannot be dealt with yet.
